.TH VOLTAIC 1 "August 2026" "voltaic" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
voltaic \- wireless device battery levels in the system tray
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B voltaic
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Voltaic
shows the charge of Logitech keyboards and mice, and of AirPods down to each
earbud and the case, in a translucent panel anchored to a tray icon. Hover
the icon to open the panel; click to keep it open.
.PP
It speaks Logitech's HID++ over
.I /dev/hidraw
and Apple's accessory protocol over an L2CAP socket directly, using only the
Python standard library. Neither Solaar nor root is required.
.PP
Only one HID++ client may poll a node at a time \(em two readers steal each
other's replies \(em so Voltaic takes a lock allowing a single instance, and
running it alongside Solaar may cause either to miss notifications.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list
Print battery levels to standard output and exit. Does not require GTK.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " SECONDS"
Seconds between background scans (default: 900). Opening the panel always
refreshes it, so a long interval only makes the tray icon and the
low-battery warning less current. See
.B POLLING
below.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-notify
Do not post low-battery notifications.
.TP
.BI \-\-tray " BACKEND"
Force a status-icon backend: one of
.BR auto ", " xembed ", " xapp ", or " appindicator .
Only
.B xembed
reports both a hover signal and the icon's screen rectangle, which is what
makes hover-to-open possible; the others fall back to a tooltip or a menu
entry. Default:
.BR auto .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH POLLING
A scan is 25 HID++ requests and 175 bytes, so the radio traffic is
irrelevant. What costs something is that pinging a sleeping device wakes it:
at the default interval that is roughly 96 wakes a day per device, a few
minutes of extra awake-but-idle time against devices rated in months.
.PP
AirPods are free while they are in the case: discovery is a D-Bus query with
no radio traffic, and the L2CAP channel is only opened for an accessory that
is already connected.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60\-voltaic.rules
Tags Logitech hidraw nodes with
.BR uaccess ,
so the logged-in user can open them. The
.B 60\-
prefix matters: systemd applies the ACL from
.IR 73\-seat\-late.rules ,
so a rules file sorting after it sets the tag too late and the node stays
.BR "root:root 0600" .
.TP
.I ~/.cache/voltaic/devices.json
Remembered names and levels, so a device that is switched off stays in the
panel with its last known charge instead of vanishing.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/voltaic.desktop
Written and removed by the
.B Start at login
entry in the tray icon's menu.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
No devices found, permission denied on the hidraw node, GTK is missing, or
another instance is already running.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR solaar (1),
.BR udev (7),
.BR getfacl (1)
.PP
Full documentation and troubleshooting:
.UR https://github.com/jcfs/voltaic
.UE
.SH BUGS
Report at
.UR https://github.com/jcfs/voltaic/issues
.UE
